<title>GERMANY: Villeroy &amp;Boch 4-mth sales, earnings up.</title>
<headline>Villeroy &amp;Boch 4-mth sales, earnings up.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>German tableware and bathroom fittings group Villeroy &amp; Boch AG said on Monday its sales and earnings had risen in the first four months of the year, boosting its hopes for 1997 as a whole.</p>
<p>Villeroy Chief Executive Joerg Grueneisen told a news conference sales in the company's three business segments had risen slightly from January to April and orders in hand were significantly higher than the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Earnings from ordinary activities in the four-month period were also significantly higher, he said.</p>
<p>Villeroy &amp; Boch reported for 1996 a net loss of 103 million marks but said last week that it expected a clear improvement in profits for 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
